  "figureNotes": [
    "Statutory amounts at IRC 129(a)(2)(A), not inflation adjusted and therefore absent from the annual revenue procedures. Pub. L. 99-514 section 1163(a) amended IRC 129(a) generally to add the limitation of exclusion, applicable to taxable years beginning after December 31, 1986 (section 1163(c)). See usc-26-129, whose 1988 amendment note quotes the pre-1988 text of paragraph (2) with the same $5,000 ($2,500) figures.",
    "Notice 2013-71 section III created the carryover option at a fixed $500 of unused amounts from a plan year, not indexed and stated in no revenue procedure. The figure belongs to the plan year the amounts are carried FROM.",
    "Notice 2012-40 section III, the unindexed statutory $2,500 amount at IRC 125(i)(1); no annual revenue procedure states a 2013 figure. Rev. Proc. 2012-41 (irb12-45) lists the 2013 adjusted items and has no Cafeteria Plans entry, because IRC 125(i)(2) indexes only for years beginning after December 31, 2013.",
    "Rev. Proc. 2013-35 section 3.15 (Cafeteria Plans).",
    "Rev. Proc. 2014-61 section 3.16 (Cafeteria Plans).",
    "Rev. Proc. 2015-53 section 3.16 (Cafeteria Plans).",
    "Rev. Proc. 2016-55 section 3.16 (Cafeteria Plans).",
    "Rev. Proc. 2017-58 section 3.16 (Cafeteria Plans). Rev. Proc. 2018-18 (irb18-10) reissued the 2018 figures after the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act changed the indexing measure, but its sections 3 and 5 list the modified and superseded sections of Rev. Proc. 2017-58 as running 3.14, 3.15, 3.18 - section 3.16 is absent - so the Cafeteria Plans figure was neither restated nor changed.",
    "Rev. Proc. 2018-57 section 3.17 (Cafeteria Plans).",
    "Notice 2020-33 section III.A raised the carryover to 20 percent of the IRC 125(i) limit for that plan year and states $550 for a plan year starting in 2020 (20 percent of $2,750). Rev. Proc. 2019-44 states no carryover figure.",
    "Rev. Proc. 2019-44 section 3.17 (Cafeteria Plans).",
    "American Rescue Plan Act of 2021, Pub. L. 117-2, section 9632(a), adding IRC 129(a)(2)(D): for a taxable year beginning after December 31, 2020 and before January 1, 2022, subparagraph (A) is applied by substituting \"$10,500 (half such dollar amount\" for \"$5,000 ($2,500\". Half of $10,500 is $5,250. Section 9632(b) applies the amendment to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2020. This is not an inflation adjustment, so no revenue procedure carries it; Rev. Proc. 2020-45 predates the March 2021 enactment and could not.",
    "Rev. Proc. section stated above, \"If the cafeteria plan permits the carryover of unused amounts, the maximum carryover amount is $550\" for taxable years beginning in 2021; the 20-percent rule itself is Notice 2020-33 (20 percent of $2750).",
    "Rev. Proc. 2020-45 section 3.17 (Cafeteria Plans).",
    "Rev. Proc. section stated above, \"If the cafeteria plan permits the carryover of unused amounts, the maximum carryover amount is $570\" for taxable years beginning in 2022; the 20-percent rule itself is Notice 2020-33 (20 percent of $2850).",
    "Rev. Proc. 2021-45 section 3.16 (Cafeteria Plans).",
    "Rev. Proc. section stated above, \"If the cafeteria plan permits the carryover of unused amounts, the maximum carryover amount is $610\" for taxable years beginning in 2023; the 20-percent rule itself is Notice 2020-33 (20 percent of $3050).",
    "Rev. Proc. 2022-38 section 3.16 (Cafeteria Plans).",
    "Rev. Proc. section stated above, \"If the cafeteria plan permits the carryover of unused amounts, the maximum carryover amount is $640\" for taxable years beginning in 2024; the 20-percent rule itself is Notice 2020-33 (20 percent of $3200).",
    "Rev. Proc. 2023-34 section 3.16 (Cafeteria Plans).",
    "Rev. Proc. section stated above, \"If the cafeteria plan permits the carryover of unused amounts, the maximum carryover amount is $660\" for taxable years beginning in 2025; the 20-percent rule itself is Notice 2020-33 (20 percent of $3300).",
    "Rev. Proc. 2024-40 section 3.16 (Cafeteria Plans).",
    "Pub. L. 119-21, section 70404(a), striking \"$5,000 ($2,500\" from IRC 129(a)(2)(A) and inserting \"$7,500 ($3,750\"; section 70404(b) applies the amendment to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025. A fixed-dollar substitution with no indexing mechanism, so no revenue procedure carries it. usc-26-129 is the 2024 edition of the Code and still prints $5,000/$2,500.",
    "Rev. Proc. section stated above, \"If the cafeteria plan permits the carryover of unused amounts, the maximum carryover amount is $680\" for taxable years beginning in 2026; the 20-percent rule itself is Notice 2020-33 (20 percent of $3400).",
    "Rev. Proc. 2025-32 section 3.15 (Cafeteria Plans)."
  ],
